==========================================
CLOUD/DEVOPS DAY 01 NOTES — LocalStack + AWS CLI
Date: 23-11-2026
==========================================

WHAT I LEARNED TODAY:
- LocalStack emulates AWS services (S3, IAM, and more) in a local Docker container
- Same aws CLI commands as real AWS; only --endpoint-url differs
- No AWS account, no credit card, no real cost or risk - fully local
- Dummy credentials ("test"/"test") work because LocalStack doesn't validate them
- S3 = object storage (buckets + objects); IAM = users/permissions

COMMANDS I PRACTICED:
[ ] localstack start -d  /  localstack status services
[ ] aws configure  (dummy creds)
[ ] awslocal s3 mb s3://day01-test-bucket
[ ] awslocal s3 cp test-file.txt s3://day01-test-bucket/
[ ] awslocal s3 cp s3://day01-test-bucket/test-file.txt downloaded/
[ ] awslocal iam create-user --user-name day01-practice-user
[ ] awslocal iam attach-user-policy ...

paste your real output here :
$ localstack status services
> 

$ awslocal s3 ls
> 


